From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LOCAL: media: iris: reload the firmware when a session
 command times out

Turning the stream off while the encoder drains, with no free capture
buffer for the firmware to finish into, hangs the Glymur video firmware:
it never answers the STOP. The driver fails that session but leaves the
firmware running, so every later session hangs too, runtime suspend fails
("skip power collapse") and only a reset of the block recovers it.

ffmpeg's h264_v4l2m2m encoder gets there by itself: while draining it
stops as soon as it holds all its capture buffers.

Reload the firmware through the existing system error work, as if the
firmware had reported the error.

Signed-off-by: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_utils.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_utils.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_utils.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_utils.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_utils.c
@@ -75,6 +75,26 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/* Firmware that misses a response answers no session any more: reload it. */
+static void iris_handle_session_timeout(struct iris_inst *inst)
+{
+	struct iris_core *core = inst->core;
+	struct iris_inst *other;
+
+	dev_err(core->dev, "session %#x timed out, reloading the firmware\n",
+		inst->session_id);
+
+	iris_inst_change_state(inst, IRIS_INST_ERROR);
+
+	mutex_lock(&core->lock);
+	core->state = IRIS_CORE_ERROR;
+	list_for_each_entry(other, &core->instances, list)
+		iris_inst_change_state(other, IRIS_INST_ERROR);
+	mutex_unlock(&core->lock);
+
+	schedule_delayed_work(&core->sys_error_handler, msecs_to_jiffies(10));
+}
+
 int iris_wait_for_session_response(struct iris_inst *inst, bool is_flush)
 {
 	struct completion *done;
@@ -86,7 +106,7 @@
 	ret = wait_for_completion_timeout(done, msecs_to_jiffies(HW_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_VALUE));
 	mutex_lock(&inst->lock);
 	if (!ret) {
-		iris_inst_change_state(inst, IRIS_INST_ERROR);
+		iris_handle_session_timeout(inst);
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
 	}
 
